From ece4786d41aa5cf2d176fcd0034178ec5c49e972 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: christopherrobertbrooks-tech
 <289533927+christopherrobertbrooks-tech@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 06:37:07 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(cuda): apply the attention score scale to the queries on
 float16 models

Eager attention, which ACE-Step uses on pre-Ampere GPUs, computes matmul(q, k^T) in the model
dtype and only then multiplies by 1/sqrt(head_dim). In the XL checkpoints decoder.layers.0's
q_norm and k_norm weights reach ~31.6 each, so one q.k over 128 dims can reach ~128,000 -- past
float16's 65,504 -- and every latent turns NaN in the XL models.

A forward hook multiplies q_norm's output by the scale (before RoPE, a rotation, which
commutes) and the module's scaling is set to 1.0: the same scores, up to float16 rounding,
come out of the matmul already scaled. It applies to every AceStepAttention (matched by class
name) in a float16 model -- all model sizes and attention backends; no weights are modified.

The fix lives in a new module (fp16_attention_scale.py); the loader calls it only when the model
dtype is float16.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
